      "dcDescription": [
        "The Magazine - S S05 Upper Volta Burkina Faso Harpa, called ngoni or ngong, of brown wood and fitted with six strings of fibre. The corpus is almost parallelepiped and has four small feet and geometric ornaments. The neck is solid wood in the shape of a slightly curved round rod. At the neck, next to the corpus, a string is attached. The stable is of curved, brown wood, through which runs on each side three strings. Used by musicians, “griots,” after war to honor the king and at other parties according to the fairytale man. Length: 85 cm. maximum width: 17 cm. Dogon. Upper Volta. (General Cata"
      ],
